repository-code: 'https://github.com/lgfachini/AutoRotOrb-ARO/'
abstract: >-
  AutoRotOrb (ARO) is a Python-based toolkit for analyzing
  ORCA Löwdin reduced orbital populations and suggesting
  molecular orbital rotations for active-space calculations.
  The program ranks molecular orbitals by selected atomic-orbital
  contributions and generates ORCA %scf rotate commands to help
  prepare CASSCF and related multireference calculations.
keywords:
  - ORCA
  - CASSCF
  - NEVPT2
  - active space
  - orbital rotation
  - Loewdin population
  - computational chemistry
